{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 47, :comments ["<b>For it is not an empty thing among you.</b> By way of the plain sense (peshat): the Holy One, blessed be He, did not command anything in the Torah in vain. And it may be interpreted as attached to 'for it is your life' (כי הוא חייכם) — it says: what I command you is not an empty thing, and even that thing which you consider to be empty, it is your life, whether in this world or in the world to come." "<b>And by way of the Midrash:</b> 'For it is not an empty thing among you' — and if it is empty, it is 'among you' (מכם), that is to say: if the reason of a matter has not become known to you, the deficiency is only from the side of the reason (sekhel) within you, that you have not reached that degree to understand it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:53:35.812194722Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}